00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.829 align:start position:0%
 
no more hiding dante  i gotta seize my moment get ready to  cross over to the land of the dead coco  provided us with an incredible story and  breathtaking visuals but it's the voice  actors that brought this film to life  let's take a look at the voices behind  our favorite characters my papa used to  sing me that song  number one  anthony gonzalez was only 12 years old  when he voiced the determined boy miguel  he was no stranger to acting however as  he had parts on criminal minds beyond  borders and fx's the bridge miguel was  the perfect fit for gonzalez as he  resonated on a personal level with the  character me and miguel are both  persevering and we never give up and we  want to do what we love gonzalez's  connection to the characters shine  through in his performance has he proved  why he was the perfect choice for the  part  i don't i don't know  i've never performed before one of  gonzalez's acting techniques was to run  in place in the recording booth if he  had to do a scene where miguel was  breathing heavily it's that kind of  commitment that makes this next fact all  the more impressive when recording the  song remember me for the touching scene  with mama coco gonzalez was actually  crying in the booth yeah we were crying  too did you know that there are three  versions of it tongue in the movie even  though we can't picture anyone else in  the role now gonzalez actually didn't  get the part right away he first  auditioned when he was just nine years  old and was initially hired to do  scratch vocal work which meant he would  be the temporary voice of the character  until the real actor was cast turns out  he was the perfect actor however as two  years later the crew surprised him with  the news that he had gotten the  permanent part they made the right  choice  number two  gael garcia bernal wished of being in a  pixar film for some time as he and his  two kids would watch pixar movies  together all the time his wish came true  when he was cast as the lovable hector  bernal loved the story and concept of  the film as he was a big fan of how they  portrayed the day of the dead  celebration they took small aspects of  different regions of mexico with a very  personal point of view around the  celebration even though hector is a  talented songwriter and singer in the  movie bernal wasn't too keen on singing  for the film they told me like  i mean you're okay singing and i was  like no well actually i'm very nervous  about it regardless of his own  trepidations bernal nailed the character  and even received high praise from his  co-star benjamin bratt his presence in  the film  lends it true authenticity number three  ernesto de la cruz was portrayed  masterfully by benjamin bratt and you my  great-great-grandson were meant to be a  musician his father was a big  inspiration for his performance but not  for any of the jealous murdery parts of  the character i thought a lot about my  own father who was a completely  different person from ernesto de la cruz  but someone who shared a similar animal  magnetism someone who walked into a room  and just commanded attention and just  had swagger and confidence much like his  co-star gael garcia-bernal brat was  nervous to sing but stated that he loves  a challenge so he was ready to take on  this daunting task the movie was also  very emotional for brat who felt the  emotional impact even before the  animation was complete i was  surprisingly and deeply moved by what i  saw  number four  jaime camille enjoyed his time playing  miguel's papa and was thrilled to be  part of such a culturally rich film  camille got emotional when watching the  film just like many others but the part  that really hit him hard is when he saw  his name in the end credits because he  realized he would be part of pixar's  prestigious catalog forever it was very  special and very touching for me all  that crying however made him have to  explain to his kids why he was so  emotional crying with them is like daddy  are you sad i'm like no i'm crying out  of happiness so explaining to them is  kind of awkward  number five  the sweet and adorable mama coco was  voiced by the equally sweet and adorable  ana ofelia morgia but that was a  musician the mexican actress was 83  years old at the time of recording her  lines proving that she is still a  talented actress at that age her career  leading up to coco is a prestigious one  as she holds the record for most  nominations for best actress for the  aerial awards an award that recognizes  the best in mexican cinema she also  holds the record for most wins for best  supporting actress for the aerial awards  with such an impressive career it's no  wonder she was chosen to voice mama coco  we definitely remembered her it's okay  i'm here  who are you  number six  renee victor played miguel's  music-hating abuelita she stated she  loves doing voice work because it only  focuses on the voice and not looks which  meant she could show up to the studio  wearing anything she liked a microphone  doesn't care what you look like she  cited director lee unkrich as a big help  as he guided victor through the voice  acting process so i related more to my  mother  than to  both of my grandmothers because her mom  had a strong and energetic nature just  like the character her grandmothers not  so much no music  no music  number  seven alana ubak knew she had to bring  her a game to play mama imelda after she  saw how detail-oriented and careful the  creators were towards the film she  didn't know much about the movie when  she auditioned and initially thought the  scene it says here no one put up your  photo my family always always puts my  photo on your friend was taking place at  a dmv ubach based her performance on her  aunt and was glad she got the  opportunity to bring her aunt's  personality to life i never forgot the  timber of her voice and her inflections  it meant so much to me even though i was  three and four years old i never forgot  that accent ubbock was a huge fan of the  movie's look and feel the music the look  of it it's it's just a bowl of candy  number eight  edward james almost brought great  emotional depth to the character of  chicharron just as other cast members  stated almost reiterated how incredibly  respectful the pixar team was of the  material and he felt privileged and  honored when they offered him the role  almost was never given the story or a  full script so he knew very little about  the movie until he watched it two years  later so you can probably imagine what  happened when he watched the film  number nine  natalia cordova buckley is no stranger  to the screen but this was her first  time voice acting starring in a pixar  movie is a pretty great first experience  just like her co-stars buckley was given  very limited information about the movie  and didn't have a picture of her  character to reference for her  performance however she did know the  real life frida kahlo very well and you  could say it was fate that she got to  play her buckley was bullied when she  was a kid for her lower raspier voice  and she was discouraged from speaking up  about it that was until her father  introduced her to frida kahlo which  helped her significantly she really uh  helped me strengthen my own voice and  find find the power within my voice we  think kahlo would be proud of how  buckley portrayed her number 10  selene luna provided her voice for tia  rosita bringing an energy to the role  that fit perfectly luna is a little  person and being cast as tia was a big  deal for her being part of coco is still  very emotional for me it validated my  20-year struggle and sacrifice as a  marginalized artist within the  entertainment industry and society as a  whole luna was able to play rosita so  well because she based her performance  off of several older women in her family  who also had nervous personalities just  like rosita and luna did an amazing job  did you know coco took six years to  complete it was totally worth the wait  as it was an incredible animated feature  that raised the bar for pixar animation  the voice actors brought these  characters to life and turned in  unforgettable performances that made the  story so memorable which coco character  is your favorite

